## Intermittent VM timing races under KVM

# `blocking_write_slave` can deadlock while KVM drains PTY echo.
device/pty/pty_blocking
# Closing a VT does not always restore the expected `VT_OPENQRY` result.
device/vt/vt_ioctl

## Deterministic Linux 6.16.0 behavior differences

# Linux ext2 driver returns `EOPNOTSUPP` for `fallocate`.
fs/ext2/fallocate
# `O_DIRECT` `preadv` racing with concurrent `ftruncate` fails the buffer check.
fs/ext2/preadv_short_read
# A write crossing into an unmapped page returns a partial count instead of `EFAULT`.
fs/ext2/short_rw
# `umount` on cwd returns `EBUSY`, and Linux accepts `MNT_ID_REQ_SIZE_VER1` (`VER0 + 8`).
fs/mount/listmount
# UID 0 can write `/proc/sys/kernel/overflowuid` after dropping `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`.
fs/procfs/proc_sys_kernel
# `fallocate` on a pidfd returns `EPERM` instead of `ENODEV`.
fs/pseudofs/fallocate
# `fchmod` on a pidfd returns `EPERM` instead of `EOPNOTSUPP`.
fs/pseudofs/pseudo_inode
# For `preadv2`/`pwritev2`, `0xf0` includes `RWF_ATOMIC`/`RWF_DONTCACHE`. Linux returns `EINVAL`, but the test expects `EOPNOTSUPP`.
io/file_io/iovec_err
# Overflowing `mremap` returns `ENOMEM`, `CAP_SYS_RAWIO` maps below `mmap_min_addr`, and ext4 rejects `MAP_SYNC`.
memory/mmap/mmap_err
# Accepted TCP sockets do not inherit listener `SO_RCVTIMEO`/`SO_SNDTIMEO` changes after `connect`.
network/sockoption
# `SO_PASSCRED` on an `AF_INET` TCP socket returns `EOPNOTSUPP`.
network/sockoption_unix
# Disabling `SO_REUSEADDR` after bind makes a second bind fail with `EADDRINUSE`.
network/tcp_reuseaddr
# Linux TCP `recv` can return fewer bytes than the Asterinas ring-buffer assumption.
network/tcp_wrapped_buffer_io
# Unconnected `recv` returns `ENOTCONN` instead of `EINVAL`, and `listen` on an accepted socket succeeds.
network/unix_seqpacket_err
# `listen` on an accepted `AF_UNIX` stream socket succeeds instead of returning `EINVAL`.
network/unix_stream_err
# Inactive child `cpu.stat` emits 4 lines instead of 3.
process/cgroup.sh
# `waitpid` without `__WCLONE`/`__WALL` returns `ECHILD` for exit signal 255.
process/clone3/clone_invalid_exit_signal
# `execveat` with `AT_EMPTY_PATH` sets `comm` differently from the test expectation.
process/execve/execve_comm
# Low-address ELF case under `CAP_SYS_RAWIO` does not die with `SIGSEGV`.
process/execve/execve_err
# `setpgid(-1, pid)` returns `ESRCH` instead of `EINVAL`.
process/group_session
# `PIDFD_SELF_THREAD_GROUP` with `PIDFD_SIGNAL_PROCESS_GROUP` returns `EBADF` instead of `ESRCH`.
process/signal/pidfd_send_signal
# Signal frame `uc_stack.ss_flags` differs from the handler expectation.
process/signal/sigaltstack
# Shebang argument splitting differs and zero-length `security.capability` xattr is accepted.
security/capability/execve
